-- title:
--   A $p$-group fixes a nonzero vector in characteristic $p$
-- statement:
--   The basic lemma used by Bender–Glauberman §2 Thm 2.6 and §3: if a $p$-group $G$ acts by a representation on a finite-dimensional vector space $V$ over a field $F$ of characteristic $p$, then there is a nonzero fixed vector (`invariants ≠ ⊥`). The corresponding Gorenstein lemma (Lemma 2.6.3) has no Isaacs counterpart.
--
--   The bundle contains supporting helpers, among them `map_pow_orderOf_eq_one`, `exists_map_pow_prime_pow_eq_one`, `charP_End_of_field`, `exists_pow_sub_one_eq_zero`, `ker_ne_bot_of_pow_eq_zero` and `zpowers_normal_of_mem_center` (a subgroup generated by a central element is normal).
--
--   The bundle also proves 1 supporting lemma used by later statements.
-- source:
--   Yawara Ishida, Lean 4 formalization of the Feit–Thompson (odd order) theorem, github.com/yawara/odd-order @ 20a6fccbb63c (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/yawara/odd-order/blob/20a6fccbb63c0b138acda9f7fafd798c42f9441b/OddOrder/GroupTheory/RepresentationTheory/PGroupFixedVector.lean

